From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Youwes09 <yuvi.shen@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 12:41:04 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132: Keep the PMC power state on

PMP's firmware crashes as it starts when the PMC power state is off,
with an asynchronous abort on its first access to the display firmware's
PMGR. Nothing in Linux claims PMC, so genpd turns it off once the PMGR's
consumers have probed.

Keep it on, as for the PMP and PMS SRAM states.

Signed-off-by: Youwes09 <yuvi.shen@outlook.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-pmgr.dtsi | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-pmgr.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-pmgr.dtsi
index 6fbf09e8f981..5a14000dd604 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-pmgr.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-pmgr.dtsi
@@ -45,6 +45,8 @@ ps_pmc: power-controller@138 {
 		#power-domain-cells = <0>;
 		#reset-cells = <0>;
 		label = "pmc";
+		/* PMP's firmware uses it; no Linux device claims it. */
+		apple,always-on;
 	};
 
 	ps_pms_fpwm0: power-controller@140 {
